<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marie Antoinette</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1755–1793</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marie Antoinette (1755–1793) was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> as the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a>. A daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, she married the future king in 1770 to seal the Franco-Austrian alliance and became a target of popular hostility for her extravagance and opposition to reform. After the fall of the monarchy she was tried by the Revolutionary Tribunal and guillotined on 16 October 1793.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marie-antoinette.jpg" alt="Marie Antoinette" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Élisabeth Louise Vigée Le Brun · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louise_Elisabeth_Vig%C3%A9e-Lebrun_-_Marie-Antoinette_dit_%C2%AB_%C3%A0_la_Rose_%C2%BB_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
